{"type":"text","timestamp":1794359870625,"sessionID":"ses_e37d2cb66ffeKlDfh1f9c34oTg","part":{"id":"prt_1c82ec484001nYaRqGBYy7OH2i","messageID":"msg_1c82eb12f001mM2kJ5b6qAoUvp","sessionID":"ses_e37d2cb66ffeKlDfh1f9c34oTg","type":"text","text":"<think>TypeScript latest is 7.0.2. TypeScript 7 is the native port. It should work with `tsc --noEmit`. But to minimize risk, maybe use TypeScript 5.9.x? Let me check if 5.9.x is available: the grep above for `^5\\.9` returned nothing in the tail (I only saw 7.x). Let me check the version list properly.\n\nActually the grep pattern was `^(5\\.9|6\\.|7\\.)` and output only showed 7.1.0-dev entries at the tail — meaning 5.9 might exist earlier in the list. Let me check specifically.</think>\n\n","time":{"start":1794359870597,"end":1794359870621}}}
