{"type":"step_start","timestamp":1794360112814,"sessionID":"ses_e37d2cb66ffeKlDfh1f9c34oTg","part":{"id":"prt_1c832769f001T9lvOVY34TpOwW","messageID":"msg_1c8322dab001UiBBJl1AvwxPc2","sessionID":"ses_e37d2cb66ffeKlDfh1f9c34oTg","type":"step-start"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794360112821,"sessionID":"ses_e37d2cb66ffeKlDfh1f9c34oTg","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"write","callID":"call-bc378f35-1044-4293-99dd-dde477ed527e","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"content":"import { useState, type FormEvent } from \"react\";\nimport { ApiError, login, register, saveSession } from \"../api\";\nimport type { Session } from \"../types\";\n\ntype Mode = \"login\" | \"register\";\n\nconst inputClass =\n  \"w-full rounded-lg border border-slate-300 bg-white px-3 py-2 text-sm text-slate-900 shadow-sm outline-none transition placeholder:text-slate-400 focus:border-indigo-500 focus:ring-2 focus:ring-indigo-200\";\n\nexport default function AuthView({ onAuthenticated }: { onAuthenticated: (session: Session) => void }) {\n  const [mode, setMode] = useState<Mode>(\"login\");\n  const [username, setUsername] = useState(\"\");\n  const [password, setPassword] = useState(\"\");\n  const [error, setError] = useState<string | null>(null);\n  const [fieldErrors, setFieldErrors] = useState<Record<string, string>>({});\n  const [busy, setBusy] = useState(false);\n\n  function switchMode(next: Mode) {\n    setMode(next);\n    setError(null);\n    setFieldErrors({});\n  }\n\n  async function handleSubmit(event: FormEvent<HTMLFormElement>) {\n    event.preventDefault();\n    setBusy(true);\n    setError(null);\n    setFieldErrors({});\n    try {\n      const session =\n        mode === \"login\" ? await login(username, password) : await register(username, password);\n      saveSession(session);\n      onAuthenticated(session);\n    } catch (caught) {\n      if (caught instanceof ApiError) {\n        setError(caught.message);\n        setFieldErrors(caught.fields);\n      } else {\n        setError(\"Something went wrong. Please try again.\");\n      }\n    } finally {\n      setBusy(false);\n    }\n  }\n\n  return (\n    <main className=\"flex min-h-screen items-center justify-center bg-slate-100 px-4 py-12\">\n      <div className=\"w-full max-w-md\">\n        <div className=\"mb-8 text-center\">\n          <div className=\"mx-auto mb-4 flex h-12 w-12 items-center justify-center rounded-2xl bg-indigo-600 text-xl font-bold text-white shadow-lg shadow-indigo-600/30\">\n            T\n          </div>\n          <h1 className=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight text-slate-900\">Timesheet</h1>\n          <p className=\"mt-1 text-sm text-slate-500\">Track your time and export it to CSV.</p>\n        </div>\n\n        <div className=\"rounded-2xl bg-white p-6 shadow-xl shadow-slate-200/60 ring-1 ring-slate-200\">\n          <div className=\"mb-6 grid grid-cols-2 gap-1 rounded-xl bg-slate-100 p-1\">\n            {([\"login\", \"register\"] as const).map((value) => (\n              <button\n                key={value}\n                type=\"button\"\n                onClick={() => switchMode(value)}\n                className={`rounded-lg px-3 py-2 text-sm font-semibold transition ${\n                  mode === value\n                    ? \"bg-white text-slate-900 shadow-sm\"\n                    : \"text-slate-500 hover:text-slate-700\"\n                }`}\n              >\n                {value === \"login\" ? \"Sign in\" : \"Register\"}\n              </button>\n            ))}\n          </div>\n\n          <form onSubmit={handleSubmit} className=\"space-y-4\" noValidate>\n            <div>\n              <label htmlFor=\"username\" className=\"mb-1.5 block text-sm font-medium text-slate-700\">\n                Username\n              </label>\n              <input\n                id=\"username\"\n                name=\"username\"\n                autoComplete=\"username\"\n                value={username}\n                onChange={(event) => setUsername(event.target.value)}\n                className={inputClass}\n                placeholder=\"you\"\n              />\n              {fieldErrors.username ? (\n                <p className=\"mt-1.5 text-sm text-rose-600\">{fieldErrors.username}</p>\n              ) : null}\n            </div>\n\n            <div>\n              <label htmlFor=\"password\" className=\"mb-1.5 block text-sm font-medium text-slate-700\">\n                Password\n              </label>\n              <input\n                id=\"password\"\n                name=\"password\"\n                type=\"password\"\n                autoComplete={mode === \"login\" ? \"current-password\" : \"new-password\"}\n                value={password}\n                onChange={(event) => setPassword(event.target.value)}\n                className={inputClass}\n                placeholder=\"••••••••\"\n              />\n              {fieldErrors.password ? (\n                <p className=\"mt-1.5 text-sm text-rose-600\">{fieldErrors.password}</p>\n              ) : null}\n            </div>\n\n            {error ? (\n              <p className=\"rounded-lg bg-rose-50 px-3 py-2 text-sm text-rose-700 ring-1 ring-rose-200\">\n                {error}\n              </p>\n            ) : null}\n\n            <button\n              type=\"submit\"\n              disabled={busy}\n              className=\"w-full rounded-lg bg-indigo-600 px-4 py-2.5 text-sm font-semibold text-white shadow-sm transition hover:bg-indigo-500 focus:outline-none focus:ring-2 focus:ring-indigo-600 focus:ring-offset-2 disabled:cursor-not-allowed disabled:opacity-60\"\n            >\n              {busy ? \"Please wait…\" : mode === \"login\" ? \"Sign in\" : \"Create account\"}\n            </button>\n          </form>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n    </main>\n  );\n}\n","filePath":"/workspace/frontend/src/components/AuthView.tsx"},"output":"Wrote file successfully.","metadata":{"diagnostics":{},"filepath":"/workspace/frontend/src/components/AuthView.tsx","exists":false,"truncated":false},"title":"frontend/src/components/AuthView.tsx","time":{"start":1794360112809,"end":1794360112817}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[]}},"id":"prt_1c83276a4001Q6I7Lm7ZQePkbZ","sessionID":"ses_e37d2cb66ffeKlDfh1f9c34oTg","messageID":"msg_1c8322dab001UiBBJl1AvwxPc2"}}
{"type":"text","timestamp":1794360112843,"sessionID":"ses_e37d2cb66ffeKlDfh1f9c34oTg","part":{"id":"prt_1c83276a1001KTUaiGM011HdUL","messageID":"msg_1c8322dab001UiBBJl1AvwxPc2","sessionID":"ses_e37d2cb66ffeKlDfh1f9c34oTg","type":"text","text":"<think>Now the components. Let me write a shared `ui.ts`? No, Tailwind classes inline.\n\ncomponents/AuthView.tsx:\n\n```tsx\nimport { useState } from \"react\";\nimport { ApiError, login, register } from \"../api\";\nimport type { Session } from \"../types\";\n\nexport default function AuthView({ onAuthenticated }: { onAuthenticated: (session: Session) => void }) {\n  const [mode, setMode] = useState<\"login\" | \"register\">(\"login\");\n  const [username, setUsername] = useState(\"\");\n  const [password, setPassword] = useState(\"\");\n  const [error, setError] = useState<string | null>(null);\n  const [fieldErrors, setFieldErrors] = useState<Record<string, string>>({});\n  const [busy, setBusy] = useState(false);\n\n  async function handleSubmit(event: FormEvent) {\n    event.preventDefault();\n    setBusy(true); setError(null); setFieldErrors({});\n    try {\n      const session = mode === \"login\" ? await login(username, password) : await register(username, password);\n      saveSession(session);\n      onAuthenticated(session);\n    } catch (err) {\n      if (err instanceof ApiError) { setError(err.message); setFieldErrors(err.fields); }\n      else setError(\"Something went wrong. Please try again.\");\n    } finally { setBusy(false); }\n  }\n  ...\n}\n```\n\nRender a card with tabs.\n\ncomponents/EntryForm.tsx — quick entry.\n\ncomponents/FiltersBar.tsx — filters + export buttons.\n\ncomponents/TotalsPanel.tsx.\n\ncomponents/EntryList.tsx — table with inline editing.\n\nApp.tsx — top-level.\n\nLet me write them one by one with good Tailwind styling.\n\nFor the entry list inline editing, I'll implement the row as a component with local state:\n\n```tsx\nfunction EntryRow({ entry, onSaved, onDeleted }) {\n  const [editing, setEditing] = useState(false);\n  const [draft, setDraft] = useState({project: entry.project, description: entry.description, hours: String(entry.hours), date: entry.date});\n  const [error, setError] = useState<string|null>(null);\n  const [fieldErrors, setFieldErrors] = useState<Record<string,string>>({});\n  const [busy, setBusy] = useState(false);\n  ...\n}\n```\n\nNote: when the entry prop changes (e.g. after refetch), the draft should reset. Use `useEffect(() => setDraft(...), [entry])`? That would reset the draft while editing if the list refetches. Since we only refetch after save/delete, it's fine. Actually, I refresh the list after saving; the entry object identity changes, resetting the draft to the saved values — fine, and I set editing=false after save.\n\nLet me keep the draft local and reset when entering edit mode.\n\nDelete with confirmation: use `window.confirm`.\n\nNow the totals panel: shows a list of projects with hours and the overall total.\n\nPaging: \"Page X of Y\" with prev/next; page_size select.\n\nLet me write App.tsx to hold the dashboard.\n\nI'll put the Dashboard in components/Dashboard.tsx.\n\nLet me write all the component files now.</think>\n\n","time":{"start":1794360112801,"end":1794360112825}}}
