{"type":"text","timestamp":1794360251869,"sessionID":"ses_e37d2cb66ffeKlDfh1f9c34oTg","part":{"id":"prt_1c83495c5001PmxV4Qmu6AeHoR","messageID":"msg_1c8347865001zw8ax8Jz2hp98u","sessionID":"ses_e37d2cb66ffeKlDfh1f9c34oTg","type":"text","text":"<think>Key insight: \"If any requirement has hash options, enable hash checking.\" — `requirements` here is built from `options.requirements` (the `-r` files) plus editables. Constraints are handled separately (in `get_requirements` for constraints → they're not added to `requirements` list? Let me check: the loop above is over `options.requirements` only; constraints are parsed in a separate function `get_requirements(constraints...)`? Let me look at the broader function.\n\nActually, in this pip version, constraints are parsed via `parse_requirements(filename, finder=..., options=..., session=...)` in a separate loop earlier in the function, and constraints' `has_hash_options` are not added to `requirements`. But the error we got says flask (from requirements.txt) lacks hashes → require_hashes was enabled. So something enabled it.\n\nHmm wait — maybe the constraint parsing sets `options.require_hashes = True` globally. Look at req_file.py line 239-240:\n```python\n        if opts.require_hashes:\n            options.require_hashes = opts.require_hashes\n```\nThat's in the parsing of a single file's options (only when the file explicitly has `--require-hashes`).\n\nBut `parse_requirements(filename, ...)` — for the *requirements* file (requirements.txt, no hashes) → no. Hmm.\n\nBut the error message said hashes are missing for flask — so require_hashes was on. Where did it come from? Possibly from the constraint file: pip's `parse_requirements` for constraints is called with the same `options` object, and in req_file.py, `RequirementsFile.parse` sets `self.options.require_hashes = True` when the file contains hashes? Let me look at req_file.py around line 230-260.\n\nWait, but the traceback: the error is \"ERROR: Hashes are required in --require-hashes mode, but they are missing from some packages.\" This error comes from pip/_internal/operations/prepare.py or from the resolver when `require_hashes` is enabled and a requirement has no hash options.\n\nLet me check where require_hashes gets set to True in this flow. In req_file.py:\n\n```python\n    def get_file_content(...)\n    ...\n        if self.options.require_hashes:\n            ...\n```\n\nLet me grep for \"require_hashes = True\" in the pip source.</think>\n\n","time":{"start":1794360251845,"end":1794360251864}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794360251964,"sessionID":"ses_e37d2cb66ffeKlDfh1f9c34oTg","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"bash","callID":"call-deeb69f2-1072-4ffd-8ac9-4ccfc17f8f54","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"grep -rn \"require_hashes = True\\|require_hashes=True\" /usr/lib/python3/dist-packages/pip/_internal/ | head -20; echo ---; sed -n '225,260p' /usr/lib/python3/dist-packages/pip/_internal/req/req_file.py","timeout":30000,"workdir":"/workspace"},"output":"/usr/lib/python3/dist-packages/pip/_internal/cli/req_command.py:286:            options.require_hashes = True\n---\n    lineno: int,\n    finder: Optional[\"PackageFinder\"] = None,\n    options: Optional[optparse.Values] = None,\n    session: Optional[\"PipSession\"] = None,\n) -> None:\n    if opts.hashes:\n        logger.warning(\n            \"%s line %s has --hash but no requirement, and will be ignored.\",\n            filename,\n            lineno,\n        )\n\n    if options:\n        # percolate options upward\n        if opts.require_hashes:\n            options.require_hashes = opts.require_hashes\n        if opts.features_enabled:\n            options.features_enabled.extend(\n                f for f in opts.features_enabled if f not in options.features_enabled\n            )\n\n    # set finder options\n    if finder:\n        find_links = finder.find_links\n        index_urls = finder.index_urls\n        no_index = finder.search_scope.no_index\n        if opts.no_index is True:\n            no_index = True\n            index_urls = []\n        if opts.index_url and not no_index:\n            index_urls = [opts.index_url]\n        if opts.extra_index_urls and not no_index:\n            index_urls.extend(opts.extra_index_urls)\n        if opts.find_links:\n            # FIXME: it would be nice to keep track of the source\n            # of the find_links: support a find-links local path\n","metadata":{"output":"/usr/lib/python3/dist-packages/pip/_internal/cli/req_command.py:286:            options.require_hashes = True\n---\n    lineno: int,\n    finder: Optional[\"PackageFinder\"] = None,\n    options: Optional[optparse.Values] = None,\n    session: Optional[\"PipSession\"] = None,\n) -> None:\n    if opts.hashes:\n        logger.warning(\n            \"%s line %s has --hash but no requirement, and will be ignored.\",\n            filename,\n            lineno,\n        )\n\n    if options:\n        # percolate options upward\n        if opts.require_hashes:\n            options.require_hashes = opts.require_hashes\n        if opts.features_enabled:\n            options.features_enabled.extend(\n                f for f in opts.features_enabled if f not in options.features_enabled\n            )\n\n    # set finder options\n    if finder:\n        find_links = finder.find_links\n        index_urls = finder.index_urls\n        no_index = finder.search_scope.no_index\n        if opts.no_index is True:\n            no_index = True\n            index_urls = []\n        if opts.index_url and not no_index:\n            index_urls = [opts.index_url]\n        if opts.extra_index_urls and not no_index:\n            index_urls.extend(opts.extra_index_urls)\n        if opts.find_links:\n            # FIXME: it would be nice to keep track of the source\n            # of the find_links: support a find-links local path\n","exit":0,"truncated":false},"title":"grep -rn \"require_hashes = True\\|require_hashes=True\" /usr/lib/python3/dist-packages/pip/_internal/ | head -20; echo ---; sed -n '225,260p' /usr/lib/python3/dist-packages/pip/_internal/req/req_file.py","time":{"start":1794360251854,"end":1794360251929}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[]}},"id":"prt_1c83495c8001UnSPEg3W23XeiE","sessionID":"ses_e37d2cb66ffeKlDfh1f9c34oTg","messageID":"msg_1c8347865001zw8ax8Jz2hp98u"}}
